% A class-function attempt types the equation at *rigid* type
% variables, exactly as a single-signature equation does — and it
% allocates them in its own search branch, off a supply the branch
% seeds for itself.
%
% Neither declared signature fits. Under `tw(T) -> T` the parameter
% is a rigid `T`, and `inc` is declared only on `int`, so the call is an
% inconsistency; `:- class` cannot carry a `requiring` clause, so no
% ambient signature can rescue it. Under `tw(string) -> string` there is
% no `inc` on strings. So the equation reports one YCHR-60006.
%
% Were the attempt's declared type variables left *flexible* — which is
% what happens if the branch never seeds its rigid supply — the
% first signature would fit by binding `T` to `int`, the attempt would
% be accepted, and the error would vanish.
:- module(typecheck_class_rigid_tvar, []).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

:- function (inc(int) -> int).
inc(X) -> X.

:- class (tw(T) -> T), (tw(string) -> string).
tw(X) -> inc(X).
